# --- Live list data: personal, never committed (see README "Storage & privacy") ---
data/lists/*.json
!data/lists/*.sample.json

# Runtime data written by the scanner's output stage (routed messages and
# their reports, staged candidates). Personal data; the directories themselves
# are kept so a clean clone can run without creating them.
data/daily-brief/**
!data/daily-brief/.gitkeep
data/outbound/**
!data/outbound/.gitkeep

# Dispatcher runtime state: which messages have been handled, and the
# quarantine trail for the ones that could not be scanned. Both name real
# correspondents, so neither is committed.
data/dispatcher/**
!data/dispatcher/.gitkeep

# The operator's REAL evaluation corpus: whole messages imported from the
# outbound store, plus the frozen list context they were labelled against. This
# is the most concentrated pile of personal data in the repository -- one
# directory holding every message the scanner has ever seen -- and it exists
# only so rule changes can be measured before they ship. It is never committed.
#
# The committed corpus is the SYNTHETIC one at tests/eval-corpus/, and the split
# is enforced rather than trusted: `email_guard.eval.privacy` refuses to grade a
# real corpus git is not ignoring, and tests/test_eval_privacy.py fails the
# build if any .eml is tracked outside the synthetic directories.
data/eval-corpus/**
!data/eval-corpus/.gitkeep

# --- Rules pack auto-updater: pulled releases and its git working copy ---
#
# Derived state, not source. `rules/` is the committed pack and the seed; every
# release under here is a copy of some upstream commit of it, and `work/` is a
# sparse clone with its own `.git`. Committing any of it would put a second,
# diverging copy of the rules pack in the history.
#
# The directory itself is kept, like the data/ ones above: the dispatcher's
# ContainerSettings.validate() requires the rules mount to be a directory, and
# an absent one is created root-owned by the docker daemon -- which the
# uid-1000 updater then cannot write to.
rules-live/**
!rules-live/.gitkeep

# --- IMAP credentials: bridge-generated, never committed (README "Running the
# dispatcher against the Proton bridge"). The sample stays. ---
config/secrets.json

# --- Compose environment: holds the bridge credentials and the host paths of
# this deployment. The sample stays. ---
.env

# The bridge's own certificate, if it is copied here for the dispatcher to
# verify against. Not secret, but it is host-specific deployment state.
config/bridge-cert.pem

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
